{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":174421,"duration_api_ms":168003,"ttft_ms":2973,"ttft_stream_ms":1927,"time_to_request_ms":11,"num_turns":24,"result":"Summary of changes:\n\n- **`salt/beacons/diskusage.py`**: each mount entry's value can now be either a plain percentage (old behavior, unchanged — fires when usage rises to/above the threshold) or a dict `{min: X%, max: Y%}`. `max` reproduces the exact old semantics; `min` fires when usage drops below that percentage (flagged in the output event with a `min` key so it's distinguishable from a high-usage alert). Both can be set for one mount, or different mounts can use different alert types. Added `_to_percent()` helper shared by both checks and extended `validate()` to reject dicts lacking `min`/`max`.\n- **`tests/pytests/unit/beacons/test_diskusage.py`**: added tests for dict-form `max`, `min`-only trigger/no-trigger, and combined `min`+`max` on the same mount, plus a validation-failure case. Full suite (15 tests) passes.\n- **`changelog/68210.added.md`**: added a changelog fragment describing the new feature.\n\nExisting plain-percentage configs are untouched by the new dict-detection branch, so production configs keep working exactly as before.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"1be292e1-8d93-400e-ad1c-4ab4592139a2","total_cost_usd":0.8453564999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":42,"cache_creation_input_tokens":46842,"cache_read_input_tokens":1178745,"output_tokens":14037,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":46842,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":42,"outputTokens":14037,"cacheReadInputTokens":1178745,"cacheCreationInputTokens":46842,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8453564999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_